      "sample_index": 0,
      "text": "To determine how long it takes for the squirrel to travel 1 mile, we start by using the formula for time, which is given by:\n\n\\[\n\\text{Time} = \\frac{\\text{Distance}}{\\text{Speed}}\n\\]\n\nHere, the distance the squirrel travels is 1 mile, and the speed of the squirrel is 4 miles per hour. Plugging these values into the formula, we get:\n\n\\[\n\\text{Time} = \\frac{1 \\text{ mile}}{4 \\text{ miles per hour}}\n\\]\n\nThis simplifies to:\n\n\\[\n\\text{Time} = \\frac{1}{4} \\text{ hours}\n\\]\n\nNext, we need to convert this time from hours to minutes. Since there are 60 minutes in an hour, we multiply the time in hours by 60:\n\n\\[\n\\text{Time in minutes} = \\frac{1}{4} \\text{ hours} \\times 60 \\text{ minutes per hour}\n\\]\n\nThis simplifies to:\n\n\\[\n\\text{Time in minutes} = \\frac{60}{4} = 15 \\text{ minutes}\n\\]\n\nTherefore, the time it takes for the squirrel to travel 1 mile is \\boxed{15} minutes.",
