      "sample_index": 3,
      "text": "To determine how long it takes for the squirrel to travel 1 mile, we start by noting the squirrel's speed and the distance it needs to cover. The squirrel's speed is 4 miles per hour, and the distance is 1 mile.\n\nFirst, we calculate the time in hours it takes for the squirrel to travel 1 mile. Since speed is distance divided by time, we can rearrange this formula to find time:\n\n\\[\n\\text{Time} = \\frac{\\text{Distance}}{\\text{Speed}}\n\\]\n\nSubstituting the given values:\n\n\\[\n\\text{Time} = \\frac{1 \\text{ mile}}{4 \\text{ miles per hour}} = \\frac{1}{4} \\text{ hours}\n\\]\n\nNext, we need to convert this time from hours to minutes. Since there are 60 minutes in an hour, we multiply the time in hours by 60:\n\n\\[\n\\text{Time in minutes} = \\frac{1}{4} \\text{ hours} \\times 60 \\text{ minutes per hour} = 15 \\text{ minutes}\n\\]\n\nThus, the time it takes for the squirrel to travel 1 mile is \\boxed{15} minutes.",
